# The party fought many times by a bot that acts with every member before the turn ends. Until
# this release a bot played the leader and nobody else, so a party scenario measured a hero with
# no cards and no abilities standing still while two others were never asked.
#
# What the report checks is the bottom two lines: nothing throws, and no run reaches the turn
# limit. `wins`, `hp_left` and `turns` are printed and not checked, here more than anywhere else:
# every bot weighs the party's hp against the enemies', and three members make that heuristic worse
# rather than better: it will spend the Vestal's heal on whoever is nearest to dead, with no idea
# that keeping her alive is what wins the fight.
#
# The `hp lost` column is the party's health between them, which is what makes it worth reading
# here: the Brigands aim at whoever has the least, so a column that counted the leader alone would
# read 0 through a fight the Vestal spent on her knees. `max_hp 40` on the leader is there so the
# Vestal's Mend cannot heal him past where he started and take the column below zero.
#
# Run:  dotnet run --project src/Cantrip.Cli -- sim samples/party

scenario "The Brigand, met by a party"
  runs 200

  player hp 40 max_hp 40
  hero Crusader
  hero Vestal

  battle Brigand, Brigand

  expect no stalls
  expect no errors
